text:
Alex (CSM): Quick summary from onboarding with Beacon Labs — their web app spins up multiple microfrontends and each calls our SDK init on load. After a staged ramp to ~80 clients we saw spikes of 429s. Customer is worried about SLA and asked if this is a platform bug or their integration. Renewal conversation next week so want to get this stable.

Lina (Support Eng): Can you share the exact error and a short log window? 429s can be caused by concurrent preflight calls or by a mis-configured token pool.

Alex (CSM): They pasted this:```
[2026-03-20T19:40:02Z] WARN rate limit preflight deny tenant=beacon count=72 window=1s
[2026-03-20T19:40:02Z] ERROR http 429 preflight_token_unavailable
[2026-03-20T19:40:03Z] INFO http request /v1/generate 200 user=frontend-A UA=BeaconWeb/3.4
```

Omar (DevEx): That count=72/1s suggests many in-flight token exchange requests. Do they use the SDKauto-fetch or do they exchange tokens server-side?

Alex (CSM): They said "autoFetch: true" in multiple components and they didn't centralize tokens. Also they open iframes that each instantiate a widget.

Zoe (Solutions Eng): Recommended mitigation steps: 1) Centralize token fetch on backend for a session id. 2) Turn off auto-fetch in embedded widgets and pass token from parent frame. 3) Add small randomized delay on init in client to spread requests across 500-2000ms.

Lina (Support Eng): Also ask them to implement quick 429 handling: return cached UI state and retry init with exponential backoff so page UX is graceful. Example:```js
// retry init with jitter
let tries=0;
function safeInit(){
  tries++;
  sdk.init().catch(err=>{
    if(err.status===429 && tries<6){
      const delay = Math.min(2000, 100*Math.pow(2,tries)) + Math.random()*300;
      setTimeout(safeInit, delay);
    }
  });
}
safeInit();
```

Alex (CSM): They pushed a quick change to staging to stop auto-fetch and share tokens from the parent frame. Want to know if we can also do a temporary service-side relief while they validate.

Zoe (Solutions Eng): We can create a short change to increase the per-tenant preflight window from 80/s -> 320/s for 4 hours. Recommend pairing with monitoring on error-rate and latency. I can own the change if ops agrees.

infra-bot: Change request CR-7920 opened: preflight quota increase for tenant=beacon, 20:00-00:00 UTC. Notifying #eng-oncall.

Omar (DevEx): I'll add a note in our onboarding checklist and docs: "If you use microfrontends/iframes, avoid per-component token fetch. Use session-scoped tokens or postMessage token sharing." Also adding a one-paragraph snippet on graceful retry UX.

Alex (CSM): I logged the impact in the account health notes and added a risk tag for renewal touch base. I'll coordinate a demo with Beacon to show the fix and ask them to validate by 23:30 UTC.

Lina (Support Eng): Once they validate, please reply here so we can close CR-7920. If errors persist we'll consider keeping the bump longer or doing a tenant migration to a larger pool.

Omar (DevEx): Also captured customer feedback: they want clearer SDK defaults documented and an opt-in example for single-token-per-session. Putting that on our quarter roadmap for DevEx content.

Alex (CSM): Thanks team 44d I'll update Beacon and follow up after their validation.
